# SSP 5.1 (5727-SS6) volume generated from the 5 1/4-inch distribution set
# (SSPMRI VOL01-02, SSPBASE VOL05-07, microcode DSKT12) on the Advanced/36
# model.  Paths are relative to this command file.  `overlay`: writes stay in
# memory and the file is never modified.
#
# The machine is left PAUSED after the poke below; attach a 5250 client to
# 127.0.0.1:2323 (the multiplexer, moved off 2300 so this machine can run
# beside the Advanced/36 one) and type `start` at the prompt.  The IPL is
# attended: the console (`console` / `console put` / `console send`) gets
# the IPL SIGN ON panel.
#
# This SSP's #MSNIP requires the system-entry customize byte at guest 0x0850
# to be 8B or 8D, else it takes its "Invalid SSP" exit.  A real machine
# derives that byte from the unit definition table it regenerates at
# power-on; this volume has none, so the byte is preset here.  Expect one
# SYS-3922 (microcode level table not written).

do ../etc/sim36.sim
attach disk0 volumes/ssp51.img overlay
set machine ipl-type attend
set terminal multiplex listen 127.0.0.1:2323

ipl pause
poke 0850 8D
